Here is my complete report on owner creation and auditing in this Spring Boot PetClinic REST repository.

## Overview
Spring Boot 4.1.0 (Maven, `spring-boot-starter-parent`), Java-based Spring MVC REST app. The `OwnerDto` and API interfaces are **generated at build time** from `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` by the OpenAPI Generator Maven plugin (7.23.0) — they don't exist as checked-in source. Owner "derived" fields (customerCode, membershipLevel, membershipNumber, etc.) are populated on the way out by a stack of AspectJ `@AfterReturning` advices.

---

## 1. Owner creation logic

**Primary creation endpoint** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, method `addOwner` (lines 103-116):
```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
@Override
public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
    HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
    owner.setCustomerCode(CustomerCode.of(owner, this.clinicService.findAllOwners()));
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
    AUDIT.info("owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}",
        owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());
    OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
        .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
}
```

**Service layer** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`, `saveOwner` (lines 233-238):
```java
@Override
@Transactional
public void saveOwner(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException {
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
}
```
Interface: `ClinicService.java`. There is no `OwnerService` class — the facade is `ClinicService`/`ClinicServiceImpl`.

**Uniqueness guard on create** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/OwnerIdentityUniquenessAspect.java`. A `@Before` advice on `ClinicService.saveOwner(..)` rejects (HTTP 409) a new owner whose `OwnerIdentity.key` (normalized telephone|email|householdId) matches an existing non-deleted owner (lines 43-55).

**V2 controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV2.java`) only lists owners (paged) — no creation.

---

## 2. How audit logging works (AUDIT references)

Two independent emitters, both using `LoggerFactory.getLogger("AUDIT")`:

**(a) Inline in the controller** — `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` line 58 declares `private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger("AUDIT");` and line 110-111 emits (shown above): a plain human-readable line `"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}"`.

**(b) Dedicated aspect** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/OwnerCreateAuditAdvice.java` (full body):
```java
@Aspect
@Component
@Order(0)
public class OwnerCreateAuditAdvice {

    private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger("AUDIT");

    @AfterReturning(pointcut = "execution(* org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.controller.v1."
        + "OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(..))", returning = "response")
    public void auditCreatedOwner(ResponseEntity<?> response) {
        if (!(response != null && response.getBody() instanceof OwnerDto owner)) {
            return;
        }
        AUDIT.info("owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={} membershipNumber={}",
            owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),
            owner.getMembershipLevel(), owner.getMembershipNumber());
    }
}
```
`@Order(0)` (highest precedence) makes this after-returning advice run last, so it observes membership fields set by the other advices.

Note: **both** current AUDIT lines are the free-text `"owner created ..."` form. Neither emits a structured event nor the marker string `OWNER_CREATED` (see gap flagged in section 5).

---

## 3. References to customerCode / membershipLevel / memberId / ownerId

- **customerCode**: model field in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` (`@Column(name="customer_code")`, getter/setter lines 64-114). Built by `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/CustomerCode.java` — format `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city, SHA-256 hash8 of telephone+lastName, with `dedupe` appending `-<n>` on collision). Also in `openapi.yml` (line 2131) and both AUDIT lines.
- **membershipLevel / membershipPoints**: derived in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/MembershipPoints.java` (`assign(...)` sets points and level 1-4, lines 36-42), capped by `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/MembershipCeiling.java`, wired via `OwnerNamesakeCountAdvice.addNamesakeCount` (lines 55-57). Schema at `openapi.yml` line 2210.
- **membershipNumber**: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/OwnerMembershipNumberAdvice.java` — format `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (line 44-45).
- **memberId**: **not present anywhere in production code.** The only occurrence is a comment in the acceptance test (see section 5) describing a *future* switch of the event's primary identifier from `customerCode` to `memberId`.
- **ownerId**: used as method params (`getOwner(Integer ownerId)`, etc.) in the V1 controller, and as `owner_id` in JDBC repos (`JdbcPet.java`, `JdbcPetRowMapper.java`, `JdbcPetRepositoryImpl.java`, `JdbcVisitRepositoryImpl.java`) and `PetMapper.java` (`@Mapping(... target="ownerId")`). No dedicated "ownerId" concept beyond the entity id.

---

## 4. Existing structured event emission / "AUDIT:" logger

There is a dedicated logger named `"AUDIT"` (used in the two places in section 2), but **no structured (JSON/key-value object) event is emitted** and there is no `"AUDIT:"` prefixed message. Current output is SLF4J parameterized free text only (`"owner created id=... "`). No `OWNER_CREATED` marker, no `seq`/`event` fields are produced yet. The test harness captures this logger via `AuditLogCapture` (section 5).

---

## 5. Test files for owners / auditing

All under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/`:

**`AcceptanceTest.java`** — the audit-event checkpoint. Full test method (lines 11-23):
```java
/** audit-event: besides the audit line, emit a structured event via AUDIT
 * {seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event:'OWNER_CREATED'}. The event must carry the
 * owner id AND the current primary identifier (customerCode here); asserting the identifier is what
 * lets later checkpoints prove the event switched to the memberId. */
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {

    @Test
    void coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier() throws Exception {
        try (AuditLogCapture audit = new AuditLogCapture()) {
            int id = createOwnerOk(knownOwner("Sydney"));
            JsonNode r = fetchOwner(id);
            // one AUDIT event line must contain the marker, the owner id and the customerCode
            assertTrue(audit.anyContains("OWNER_CREATED", String.valueOf(id),
                    r.get("customerCode").asText()));
        }
    }
}
```
This asserts a single `AUDIT` line contains all of `OWNER_CREATED`, the owner id, and the customerCode. The current emitters (section 2) do NOT contain the `OWNER_CREATED` marker — so this checkpoint targets adding a structured event carrying `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event:'OWNER_CREATED'}`.

**`AuditLogCapture.java`** — an `AutoCloseable` that attaches a Logback `ListAppender` to the `AUDIT` logger. Key methods: `anyContains(String... substrings)` (all substrings must appear in one message, lines 45-54), `anyAtLevel(level, substrings...)` (lines 57-69), `messages()`, `count()`. Default constructor targets logger name `"AUDIT"`.

**`AcceptanceBase.java`** — `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(roles={"OWNER_ADMIN","VET_ADMIN","ADMIN"})`. Black-box helpers all hit `POST /api/owners` + `GET /api/owners/{id}`: `createOwner`/`createOwnerOk`/`createOwnerWithKey`, `ownerNode()` (fully-valid unique payload), `knownOwner(city)`, `structuredOwner()`, `fetchOwner(id)`, `extractId(...)`, plus pinned reference data (CITY_REGION, REGION_POSTCODES, HOLIDAYS) and algorithm replicas (`sha256hex`, `shaHex`, `luhn`). Tests roll back per-test via `@Transactional`.

---

## 6. Build system and running tests

- **Maven** (no Gradle). Wrapper present: `/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw` (+ `mvnw.cmd`), `pom.xml`, `.mvn/`.
- Parent: `spring-boot-starter-parent` **4.1.0**. Tests use `spring-boot-starter-test`, `spring-boot-starter-webmvc-test`, `spring-boot-starter-security-test` (JUnit 5 / MockMvc). Logback is the logging backend (relied on by `AuditLogCapture`).
- **DTOs/API are generated at build time** by the `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` (7.23.0) from `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` into `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto` / `...rest.api`. You must run a Maven build (not just javac) for `OwnerDto`, `OwnersApi`, etc. to exist.
- Run tests: `./mvnw test` (full verify: `./mvnw clean install`; single class: `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest`). Run app: `./mvnw spring-boot:run` (readme line 25).

Note: I am in read-only mode and did not execute any build or test commands.

